## The Boundary

Pregnancy creates an extraordinary connection between two organisms.

Yet the boundary between them remains real.

Oxygen crosses.

Glucose crosses.

Amino acids cross.

Some fatty acids cross.

Some medications cross.

Some environmental contaminants cross.

Maternal antibodies can be actively transferred.

Glucocorticoids are metabolized and regulated.

Immune signals move through multiple pathways.

But transfer is selective.

The maternal circulation is not the fetal circulation.

Maternal exposure is not fetal dose.

And fetal dose is not developmental outcome.

This sequence is perhaps the single most useful piece of biological vocabulary a parent can acquire.

**Exposure.**

**Transfer.**

**Dose.**

**Response.**

**Outcome.**

Each is a different question.

The mistake is to collapse them into one.

